{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AUTO-HEAL: the exact gap, and a safer rule than my earlier 'hard-reset if no unpushed commits'.\n\n`_store/event_append.py:_recover_from_unmerged` (line ~671) ALREADY auto-heals a stranded\nindex — but its classifier has only TWO buckets:\n    _REGENERABLE_PREFIX = '.bridge_state/'        (line 668)\n    nonregen = [p for p in unmerged if not p.startswith(_REGENERABLE_PREFIX)]   (line 692)\nAnything not under `.bridge_state/` is assumed to be TICKET DATA and the write is refused.\n\nTonight's unmerged paths were `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` and\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py`. Those are a THIRD kind the classifier has no bucket\nfor: files that do not belong on the tickets branch AT ALL. They are not regenerable, but they\nare also emphatically not ticket data — `origin/tickets` tracks no source tree whatsoever\n(verified: `ls-tree origin/tickets` returns only ticket dirs plus .bridge_state,\n.gitattributes, .gitignore, .pre-commit-config.yaml, .store-compat.json, .ticket-write.lock).\nSo they fell into `nonregen` and wedged EVERY store write until a human intervened.\n\nBETTER RULE (safer than my earlier suggestion of hard-resetting when no unpushed commits\nexist, which discards more than necessary and needs a broader safety argument):\n\n    An unmerged path that the tickets branch does not track, and that is not shaped like a\n    ticket path, CANNOT be ticket data — so discard it exactly as the regenerable case does.\n\nClassify FOREIGN as: not present in HEAD's tree AND not matching a ticket directory\n(`^[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f-]+/`) AND not one of the known store dotfiles. That is conservative by\nconstruction — it auto-discards only paths that provably do not belong to the store — and it\nwould have healed tonight's wedge with zero human involvement, while still refusing on a\ngenuine conflict inside real ticket data.\n\nKeep the existing refuse-and-surface behaviour for anything that IS ticket-shaped. The point of\nauto-heal is to remove the need to reach for raw git, which is what caused the collateral\ndamage in the first place.\n\nAcceptance criteria to add:\n- [ ] `_recover_from_unmerged` gains a FOREIGN-path bucket (not tracked on the tickets branch,\n      not ticket-shaped, not a known store dotfile) that is discarded like the regenerable case.\n- [ ] A genuine unmerged path INSIDE a ticket directory still refuses and surfaces.\n- [ ] Held-out tests for both directions, using tonight's exact paths as the foreign fixture."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786329913796634001,"uuid":"5d34a778-5ac8-428e-84df-c3674b311b1c"}